    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d770">

                <pb facs="0674" n="598" xml:id="pg598"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 812.00/18609</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the Secretary of War </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Department of State</hi>, <lb/>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1916-07-01">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">July 1, 1916</hi></date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>
                    <hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have the honor to enclose herewith a
                    copy of a letter from the representative in Washington of the <hi
                        rendition="#italic">de facto</hi> Government of Mexico, in regard to the
                    reported arrest of certain inhabitants of La Cruz, Mexico, by troops under the
                    command of General Pershing, and to alleged outrages by Apaches attached to
                    General Pershing’s forces.</p>
                <p>The Department would be glad to receive from you a report in regard to the
                    matter.</p>
                <p>I have [etc.]</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Robert Lansing</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
